{:edb/db-before-t 2607 :edb/db-after-t 2608 :edb/tx-data [[13194139535920 50 #inst "2026-10-09T10:41:45.092Z" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179512 1100 "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5]$. If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1}$, calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j$." 13194139535920 false] [17592186179512 1100 "Let $P= \\left\\{y_0, y_1, \\ldots, y_n\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 5].$ If $\\Delta y_j = y_j - y_{j-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n {3}\\Delta y_j.$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179512 1145 "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}3Δ{y}_{j}=3{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j$ is just the length of the interval $[-3, 5],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{j=1}^{n}Δ{y}_{j} & =Δ{y}_{1}+Δ{y}_{2}+Δ{y}_{3}+⋯+Δ{y}_{n} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}-{y}_{0})+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})+({y}_{3}-{y}_{2})+⋯+({y}_{n}-{y}_{n-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{y}_{1}}-{y}_{0})+(\\cancel{{y}_{2}}-\\cancel{{y}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{y}_{3}}-\\cancel{{y}_{2}})+⋯+({y}_{n}-\\cancel{{y}_{n-1}}) \\\\  & =-{y}_{0}+{y}_{n} \\\\  & ={y}_{n}-{y}_{0} \\\\  & =5-(-3) \\\\  & =5+3 \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24.\n$$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179512 1145 "First, we take the factor $3$ outside the summation:\n\n$$\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)3Δy_{j} = 3∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j}\n$$\n\nNote that\n\n$$\n\\displaystyle \\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j\n$$\n\nis just the length of the interval $[-3, 5]$, because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δy_{j} &= Δy_{1} + Δy_{2} + Δy_{3} + ⋯ + Δy_{n} \\\\\n&= (y_{1} - y_{0}) + (y_{2} - y_{1}) + (y_{3} - y_{2}) + ⋯ + (y_{n} - y_{n - 1}) \\\\\n&= (y_{1} - y_{0}) + (y_{2} - y_{1}) + (y_{3} - y_{2}) + ⋯ + (y_{n} - y_{n - 1}) \\\\\n&=-y_{0} + y_{n} \\\\\n&= y_{n} - y_{0} \\\\\n&= 5 - (-3) \\\\\n&= 5 + 3 \\\\\n&= 8\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{3}\\sum_{j=1}^n \\Delta y_j = 3 \\cdot 8 = 24\n$$" 13194139535920 false] [17592186179513 1100 "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4]$. If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1}$, calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i$." 13194139535920 false] [17592186179513 1100 "Let $P = \\left\\{x_0, x_1, \\ldots, x_m\\right\\}$ be a partition of the interval $[-3, 4].$ If $\\Delta x_i = x_i - x_{i-1},$ calculate $\\displaystyle\\sum_{i=1}^m (x_i + x_{i-1})\\Delta x_i .$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179513 1145 "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= (x_{1} + x_{0})Δx_{1} + (x_{2} + x_{1})Δx_{2} + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})Δx_{m} \\\\\n&= (x_{1} + x_{0})(x_{1} - x_{0}) + (x_{2} + x_{1})(x_{2} - x_{1}) + ⋯ + (x_{m} + x_{m - 1})(x_{m} - x_{m - 1}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&= (x_{1}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}) + (x_{2}^{2} - x_{1}^{2}) + ⋯ + (x_{m}^{2} - x_{m - 1}^{2}) \\\\\n&=-x_{0}^{2} + x_{m}^{2} \\\\\n&= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i} &= x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2} \\\\\n&= 4^{2} - (-3)^{2} \\\\\n&= 7\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535920 false] [17592186179513 1145 "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{m} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $x_0 = -3$ and $x_m = 4$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={4}^{2}-(-3)^{2} \\\\  & =7.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179515 1100 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]$?\n\n1. $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n2. $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n3. $1 < 2 < 9$" 13194139535920 false] [17592186179515 1100 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[1,9]?$\n\n- $\\{1, 4, 5, 8\\}$\n\n- $\\{1, 3, 4, 9\\}$\n\n- $1 <     2  <    9$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179515 1145 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 <      x_1<      x_2 <      \\ldots <      x_n = b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9.$\n\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9].$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179515 1145 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na = x_0 < x_1< x_2 < \\ldots < x_n = b\\,\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP=\\{x_0,x_1,\\ldots,x_n\\}\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[1,9]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=9$.\n- Statement II is a partition of $[1,9]$.\n- Statement III is a partition of $[1,9]$.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"" 13194139535920 false] [17592186179650 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374430 13194139535920 true] [17592186179650 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374437 13194139535920 true] [17592186179650 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374444 13194139535920 true] [17592186179650 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374451 13194139535920 true] [17592186179651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374458 13194139535920 true] [17592186179651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374465 13194139535920 true] [17592186179651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374472 13194139535920 true] [17592186179651 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374479 13194139535920 true] [17592186179653 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374395 13194139535920 true] [17592186179653 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374402 13194139535920 true] [17592186179653 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374409 13194139535920 true] [17592186179653 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374416 13194139535920 true] [17592186179653 1020 #edb/ref 17592186374423 13194139535920 true] [17592186179905 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535920 true] [17592186179905 1100 "Let $P = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0, 3]$. If $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$, calculate $∑_(i = 1)^(m)5Δx_{i}$." 13194139535920 false] [17592186179905 1100 "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,3].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}.$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179905 1145 "Using the constant multiple rule, we can write the summation as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}5Δ{x}_{i}=5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}$ is just the length of the interval $[0,3],$ because\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+({x}_{3}-{x}_{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}}-{x}_{0})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}})+(\\cancel{{x}_{3}}-\\cancel{{x}_{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}+{x}_{m} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}-{x}_{0} \\\\  & =3-0 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n5{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}Δ{x}_{i}=5\\cdot 3=15.\n$$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179906 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139535920 true] [17592186179906 1100 "Let $P = {x_{0}, x_{1}, …, x_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0, 2]$. If $Δx_{i} = x_{i} - x_{i - 1}$, calculate $∑_(i = 1)^(m)(x_{i} + x_{i - 1})Δx_{i}$." 13194139535920 false] [17592186179906 1100 "Let $P={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{m}}$ be a partition of the interval $[0,2].$ If $Δ{x}_{i}={x}_{i}-{x}_{i-1},$ calculate ${\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i}.$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186179906 1145 "We can simplify the given summation as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})Δ{x}_{1}+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})Δ{x}_{2}+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})Δ{x}_{n} \\\\  & =({x}_{1}+{x}_{0})({x}_{1}-{x}_{0})+({x}_{2}+{x}_{1})({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})+⋯+({x}_{m}+{x}_{m-1})({x}_{m}-{x}_{m-1}) \\\\  & =({x}_{1}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2})+({x}_{2}^{2}-{x}_{1}^{2})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{m-1}^{2}) \\\\  & =(\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}}-{x}_{0}^{2})+(\\cancel{{x}_{2}^{2}}-\\cancel{{x}_{1}^{2}})+⋯+({x}_{m}^{2}-\\cancel{{x}_{m-1}^{2}}) \\\\  & =-{x}_{0}^{2}+{x}_{m}^{2} \\\\  & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since ${x}_{0}=0$ and ${x}_{m}=2$ are the endpoints of our partition, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{m}({x}_{i}+{x}_{i-1})Δ{x}_{i} & ={x}_{m}^{2}-{x}_{0}^{2} \\\\  & ={2}^{2}-{0}^{2} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374395 1017 #edb/ref 17592186374396 13194139535920 true] [17592186374395 1089 "q-122932" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374395 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535920 true] [17592186374395 1100 "Which of the following are partitions of the real interval $[-4,6]?$\n\n- $-5<-4<-2<0<4<6$\n- ${-3,3,5,6}$\n- ${-4,4,5}$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374395 1113 #uuid "d62099c6-5c34-55aa-ad1f-5500db9aeb0d" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374395 1145 "A partition $P$ of a closed interval $[a,b]$ is a finite sequence of real numbers taken from $[a,b]$ such that\n\n$$\na={x}_{0}<{x}_{1}<{x}_{2}<…<{x}_{n}=b\\,.\n$$\n\nWe can express $P$ using set notation as\n\n$$\nP={{x}_{0},{x}_{1},…,{x}_{n}}.\n$$\n\n \n\nWith that in mind, let's consider each statement:\n\n- Statement I is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since $-5$ does not belong to $[-4,6].$\n\n- Statement II is not a partition of $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the left endpoint $a=-4.$\n\n- Statement III is not a partition of  $[-4,6]$ since it does not include the right endpoint $b=6.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6].$\"" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374397 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374398 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374399 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374400 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1000 #edb/ref 17592186374401 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1041 "selection" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1104 #edb/ref 17592186374398 13194139535920 true] [17592186374396 1110 #uuid "f39795d1-aea8-5b4e-af92-aa80c6697c45" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374397 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374397 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535920 true] [17592186374397 1111 #uuid "40293fdb-f0b0-5105-8166-5fa2eec997ff" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374398 1034 "None of the statements give a partition of  $[-4,6]$" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374398 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535920 true] [17592186374398 1111 #uuid "705e3f09-0324-5d64-b4d3-c4b01cd4d956" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374399 1034 "I only" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374399 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535920 true] [17592186374399 1111 #uuid "41ec46a2-2751-59e3-aa6d-66be9ef35514" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374400 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535920 true] [17592186374400 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535920 true] [17592186374400 1111 #uuid "0a9dc897-08ac-5e0e-ad55-9c020ba9dba0" 131941